ICML-2024-P0601,ICML-2024-A002889,Dan Garber,shared,3,2,2,"(throughout all rounds) feasible convex set K ⊂ Rn , which we will also assume to be compact (as is often standard). After choosing xt , a scalar loss ft (xt ) is incurred, where ft : Rn → R is some arbitrary convex loss function (assumed for sake of analysis to be chosen adversarially). The standard goal is, on the course of the T rounds, to choose feasible actions PxT1 , . . . , xT such that the PTregret, given by the difference t= ft (xt ) − minx∈K t= ft (x), grows (as a function of T ) only at a sublinear rate (the slower the better).",-4,data/raw/icml/2024/first_pages/ICML-2024-P0601.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v235/main/assets/garber24a/garber24a.pdf
