ICML-2024-P0722,ICML-2024-A003469,Hao-Yuan He,shared,3,4,4,"Abductive Learning (ABL) (Zhou, ; Dai et al., ) represents a novel framework seamlessly integrating machine learning systems with logical reasoning systems. Within this framework, the machine learning model is trained to transform raw input data, e.g., images and text, into sub-symbolic concepts; concurrently, the logical model is designed to conduct reasoning based on these concepts. Logical reasoning, facilitated through abductive reasoning (Magnani, ), is employed to identify the accurate concepts of unlabeled instances; these identified concepts are then utilized to update the machine learning model through supervised learning.",-4,data/raw/icml/2024/first_pages/ICML-2024-P0722.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v235/main/assets/he24j/he24j.pdf
