ICML-2024-P1242,ICML-2024-A006203,Yuxing Liu,shared,3,3,3,"where each component function fi,j : Rd → R is smooth and convex, and n is number of components on every node. We focus on first-order decentralized optimization methods that desire all the m nodes to minimize the global objective cooperatively, which allows each node to access its local incremental first-order oracle (LIFO) and communicate with its neighbors. This problem setting is very popular in training machine learning models with large amounts of data samples.",-4,data/raw/icml/2024/first_pages/ICML-2024-P1242.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v235/main/assets/liu24i/liu24i.pdf
