ICML-2024-P1587,ICML-2024-A007921,Jiarong Pan,shared,3,4,4,"BO. In this context, each task denotes the optimization of a specific black-box function and we assume that related tasks share similarities with the target task. For instance, one can warm-start the tuning of a neural network when the same network was previously tuned on related datasets. Previous runs on related tasks can be used to build informed surrogate models (Perrone et al., ; Wistuba & Grabocka, ; Feurer et al., ), restrict the search space (Perrone et al., ), or initialize the optimization with configurations that generally score well (Feurer et al., ; Volpp et al., ).",-6,data/raw/icml/2024/first_pages/ICML-2024-P1587.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v235/main/assets/pan24b/pan24b.pdf
