ICML-2024-P2084,ICML-2024-A010245,Yasen Wang,shared,3,4,4,"where y ∈ Rn is the output vector, Φ(x) ∈ Rn×m is the overcomplete dictionary matrix composed of basis functions on the input vector x, w ∈ Rm is the unknown weight vector, and ε is the uncorrelated Gaussian noise distributed as N ( , λIn ) with the unknown variance λ. Notably, realizing sparse recovery for w is a fundamental problem in machine learning communities with applications to various science and engineering disciplines, such as signal processing (Donoho, ; Kümmerle et al., ; Ament & Gomes, 2021a), system identification (Yuan et al., ; Sun et al., ; ; Wang et al., ), and regression and classification tasks (Figueiredo, ; Ren et al., ). Consequently, it is particularly important to design an optimization method with rigorous theoretical guarantees for solving ( ) given the sparse constraint on w.",-10,data/raw/icml/2024/first_pages/ICML-2024-P2084.txt,https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v235/main/assets/wang24al/wang24al.pdf
